; ==========================================================================
; STELLAR STARSHIP v02  -  the COSMAC ELF logo, steered with the arrow keys
; ==========================================================================
; The picture is painted once, then slides left or right round the screen,
; wrapping at the edges:
;
;   RIGHT ARROW   one step faster to the right (slower, if it is going left)
;   LEFT ARROW    one step faster to the left  (slower, if it is going right)
;   SPACE         stop
;   Q             quit - restores the cursor and clears the screen
;
; d and a do the same as the arrows, for terminals that send none.  The more
; presses, the faster it goes: speed is columns per frame, 0 to 9, shown on
; line 1 as a row of > or < marks.  Press the other arrow to slow it down,
; through a stop, and away the other way.
;
; NEEDS A VT102-CLASS TERMINAL.  The picture is not redrawn to move it - that is
; about 1300 bytes, over a second at 9600 baud.  Each of its 21 lines is shifted
; IN THE TERMINAL with the VT102 character insert / delete controls, ESC[n@ and
; ESC[nP (TeraTerm, PuTTY, minicom, xterm and anything calling itself VT102 or
; later have them; a strict VT100 does not), and only the n cells that wrap round
; the edge are painted.  About 190 bytes of output a frame at speed 1.
;
; Each line's control - CR LF, then ESC [ S @, or ESC [ S P ESC [ 7 u C which also
; moves the cursor to column 81-S - is ONE string, rebuilt once a frame at $4D80
; and sent with a single PRINTSTR.  The frame starts on the line above the
; picture, so each CR LF steps down one line; no cursor addressing per line.
;
; THE PICTURE GRID at $4300 keeps every picture row followed by its own first 9
; columns again, so the S cells read from any start column never need a wrap
; test.  Each grid byte is the LOW BYTE of a string in the page at $4D00: a
; blank, ESC[7m-space-ESC[0m for a lit cell, or a caption letter.  Painting a
; cell is four commands - READIDX, ADDAI, COPYAX, PRINTSTR - and leaves the
; terminal in normal video.  The first paint still uses the run table at $4B00
; (line, first column, length), as v01 did.
;
; REGISTERS.  R0 = 0 (the WRITEIDX index), R1 the picture offset (0-79), R2 the
; speed, R3 the direction (1 right, 0 left), R4 lines left to shift, R5 the grid
; row, R7 cells left to paint, R8 the constant 80, R9 the first wrapped column,
; RA the grid index, RB key-state / string pointer, RC the key, RD/RE line and
; column for POSXY, RF the constant ten.  R0 is loaded through the accumulator:
; $11 LOADXI cannot write it.
;
; SIM-VERIFIED on V0061.30 (Firmware-Math/starship_verify.py): the serial stream
; is replayed into an 80x23 VT102 screen and at the start of EVERY frame the
; picture lines equal Craig's pattern rotated by the offset the stream implies,
; cell for cell including reverse video - 157 frames through a session that
; speeds up right, reverses through zero, stops, goes flat out both ways and
; quits.  Frame cost: speed 1 about 54,000 1802 instructions, speed 4 about
; 125,000, speed 9 about 222,000.  NOT YET HARDWARE-VERIFIED.
;
; The pattern is Craig's, from APPLICATIONS/Starship Graphic.txt (edit that file
; and rerun Firmware-Math/gen_starship.py, not this listing):
;
;   |                                                                                |
;   |   ##### ##### ##### #   # ##### #####                                          |
;   |   #   # #   # #     ## ## #   # #   #                                          |
;   |   #     #   # ##### # # # ##### #                                              |
;   |   #   # #   #     # #   # #   # #   #                                          |
;   |   ##### ##### ##### #   # #   # #####                                          |
;   |                                                                  ########      |
;   |                                        ########################################|
;   |                 ###                   ##                                     ##|
;   |            #############              ##                                    ## |
;   |  ############         ############     ########  ############################# |
;   |  #             #####             ##           #  ##                            |
;   |  ############         ############            #  ##                            |
;   |             ##########  ##     ##             #  ##                            |
;   |                #####     ##     ##            #  ##         ##### #     #####  |
;   |                           ##     ##           #  ##         #     #     #      |
;   |                         #######################  #####      ####  #     ####   |
;   |                       ####                          ###     #     #     #      |
;   |                      ####  ###########               ##     ##### ##### #      |
;   |                       ###                 #############                        |
;   |                        ####       #########                                    |
;   |                           #########                         STELLAR EDITION    |
;   |                                                                                |
;
; 235 STELLAR commands, $4000-$428A (651 bytes of code).
; Data at $4300, 2047 bytes, past the end marker.
; Data at $4B00, 325 bytes, past the end marker.
; Data at $4C60, 16 bytes, past the end marker.
; Data at $4C80, 61 bytes, past the end marker.
; Data at $4D00, 32 bytes, past the end marker.
; Data at $4D80, 13 bytes, past the end marker.
; Data at $4DC0, 2 bytes, past the end marker.
;
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DISASSEMBLY  -  commented out; the loader skips it
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; D 4000 CD             START                  Start of program, and run the label pre-pass
; D 4001 11 0F 00 0A    LOADXI R15 000A        Ten, for splitting numbers into digits
; D 4005 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B             Clear the screen
; D 4007 CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B
; D 4009 CA 32          SEROUTI 32
; D 400B CA 4A          SEROUTI 4A
; D 400D CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B             Hide the cursor
; D 400F CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B
; D 4011 CA 3F          SEROUTI 3F
; D 4013 CA 32          SEROUTI 32
; D 4015 CA 35          SEROUTI 35
; D 4017 CA 6C          SEROUTI 6C
; D 4019 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B             Reverse video: a space is now a lit block
; D 401B CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B
; D 401D CA 37          SEROUTI 37
; D 401F CA 6D          SEROUTI 6D
; D 4021 11 09 00 00    LOADXI R9 0000         Index into the run table
; NEXT:
; D 4025 2E 09 0B 00    READIDX R9 0B00        The line this run sits on
; D 4029 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000            Zero ends the table
; D 402C A0 00 52       IFTRUEI SHOWN
; D 402F 21 0D          COPYAX 0D              into R13 for POSXY
; D 4031 42 09          INCX R9
; D 4033 2E 09 0B 00    READIDX R9 0B00        The column it starts at
; D 4037 21 0E          COPYAX 0E              into R14
; D 4039 42 09          INCX R9
; D 403B 2E 09 0B 00    READIDX R9 0B00        and how many cells long it is
; D 403F 21 0A          COPYAX 0A              into R10
; D 4041 42 09          INCX R9
; D 4043 BD 02 69       CALL POSXY
; RUN:
; D 4046 CA 20          SEROUTI 20             A space in reverse video is a lit block
; D 4048 43 0A          DECX R10
; D 404A 8C 0A          TESTXZ R10
; D 404C A1 00 46       IFFALSEI RUN
; D 404F B0 00 25       GAL NEXT
; SHOWN:
; D 4052 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B             Normal video for the caption and the help line
; D 4054 CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B
; D 4056 CA 30          SEROUTI 30
; D 4058 CA 6D          SEROUTI 6D
; D 405A 11 0D 00 16    LOADXI R13 0016        Caption line
; D 405E 11 0E 00 3E    LOADXI R14 003E        and column
; D 4062 BD 02 69       CALL POSXY
; D 4065 11 0B 0C 60    LOADXI R11 0C60        -> 'STELLAR EDITION'
; D 4069 C1 0B          PRINTSTR R11
; D 406B 11 0D 00 17    LOADXI R13 0017        The help line
; D 406F 11 0E 00 03    LOADXI R14 0003
; D 4073 BD 02 69       CALL POSXY
; D 4076 11 0B 0C 80    LOADXI R11 0C80
; D 407A C1 0B          PRINTSTR R11
; D 407C 10 00 00       LOADAI 0000            R0 = 0, the WRITEIDX index (LOADXI cannot write R0)
; D 407F 21 00          COPYAX 00
; D 4081 11 08 00 50    LOADXI R8 0050         R8 = 80, the width of the picture
; D 4085 11 01 00 00    LOADXI R1 0000         Offset 0 - the picture as drawn
; D 4089 11 02 00 00    LOADXI R2 0000         Speed 0 - standing still
; D 408D 11 03 00 01    LOADXI R3 0001         Direction: right
; D 4091 11 0B 0D C0    LOADXI R11 0DC0        The arrow-key state starts clear -
; D 4095 32 0B 00 00    COPYMX2I R11 0000      the pre-pass does not clear RAM
; KEYS:
; D 4099 11 0B 0D C0    LOADXI R11 0DC0        RB back on the key state - shifting borrows it
; KLOOP:
; D 409D CC             SERST                  Anything typed?
; D 409E A1 01 5B       IFFALSEI FRAME         No - on with the frame
; D 40A1 CB             SERIN
; D 40A2 21 0C          COPYAX 0C              RC = the key
; D 40A4 33 0B          COPYMXA 0B             The arrow-key state machine: an arrow is three
; D 40A6 81 00 01       TESTAI 0001            bytes, ESC [ C (right) or ESC [ D (left)
; D 40A9 A0 00 E8       IFTRUEI KST1
; D 40AC 33 0B          COPYMXA 0B
; D 40AE 81 00 02       TESTAI 0002
; D 40B1 A0 00 FA       IFTRUEI KST2
; D 40B4 86 0C 00 1B    TESTXI R12 001B        ESC starts one
; D 40B8 A1 00 C2       IFFALSEI KPLAIN
; D 40BB 32 0B 00 01    COPYMX2I R11 0001
; D 40BF B0 00 9D       GAL KLOOP
; KPLAIN:
; D 40C2 86 0C 00 20    TESTXI R12 0020        SPACE stops
; D 40C6 A0 01 51       IFTRUEI STOP
; D 40C9 86 0C 00 64    TESTXI R12 0064        d is right, for terminals that send no arrows
; D 40CD A0 01 0F       IFTRUEI GORIGHT
; D 40D0 86 0C 00 61    TESTXI R12 0061        a is left
; D 40D4 A0 01 2B       IFTRUEI GOLEFT
; D 40D7 86 0C 00 71    TESTXI R12 0071        q quits
; D 40DB A0 02 18       IFTRUEI QUIT
; D 40DE 86 0C 00 51    TESTXI R12 0051        and so does Q
; D 40E2 A0 02 18       IFTRUEI QUIT
; D 40E5 B0 00 9D       GAL KLOOP
; KST1:
; D 40E8 32 0B 00 00    COPYMX2I R11 0000      Whatever it was, the sequence restarts
; D 40EC 86 0C 00 5B    TESTXI R12 005B        Was it '[' ?
; D 40F0 A1 00 9D       IFFALSEI KLOOP
; D 40F3 32 0B 00 02    COPYMX2I R11 0002      Now expect the letter
; D 40F7 B0 00 9D       GAL KLOOP
; KST2:
; D 40FA 32 0B 00 00    COPYMX2I R11 0000      Sequence finished
; D 40FE 86 0C 00 43    TESTXI R12 0043        'C' is the right arrow
; D 4102 A0 01 0F       IFTRUEI GORIGHT
; D 4105 86 0C 00 44    TESTXI R12 0044        'D' is the left arrow
; D 4109 A0 01 2B       IFTRUEI GOLEFT
; D 410C B0 00 9D       GAL KLOOP
; GORIGHT:
; D 410F 8C 02          TESTXZ R2              Standing still?
; D 4111 A0 01 20       IFTRUEI SETR
; D 4114 86 03 00 01    TESTXI R3 0001         Already going right?
; D 4118 A0 01 45       IFTRUEI FASTER
; D 411B 43 02          DECX R2                No - going left, so slow down
; D 411D B0 01 55       GAL SHOWK
; SETR:
; D 4120 11 03 00 01    LOADXI R3 0001         Start moving right
; D 4124 11 02 00 01    LOADXI R2 0001         at speed 1
; D 4128 B0 01 55       GAL SHOWK
; GOLEFT:
; D 412B 8C 02          TESTXZ R2              Standing still?
; D 412D A0 01 3A       IFTRUEI SETL
; D 4130 8C 03          TESTXZ R3              Already going left?
; D 4132 A0 01 45       IFTRUEI FASTER
; D 4135 43 02          DECX R2                No - going right, so slow down
; D 4137 B0 01 55       GAL SHOWK
; SETL:
; D 413A 11 03 00 00    LOADXI R3 0000         Start moving left
; D 413E 11 02 00 01    LOADXI R2 0001         at speed 1
; D 4142 B0 01 55       GAL SHOWK
; FASTER:
; D 4145 86 02 00 09    TESTXI R2 0009         Already flat out?
; D 4149 A0 01 55       IFTRUEI SHOWK
; D 414C 42 02          INCX R2                One step faster
; D 414E B0 01 55       GAL SHOWK
; STOP:
; D 4151 11 02 00 00    LOADXI R2 0000         Speed 0
; SHOWK:
; D 4155 BD 02 3D       CALL SPEED             Show the new speed on line 1
; D 4158 B0 00 99       GAL KEYS               and see if there is more typing
; FRAME:
; D 415B 8C 02          TESTXZ R2              Standing still?
; D 415D A1 01 65       IFFALSEI MOVE
; D 4160 C0 04          DLYI 04                Yes - idle a moment and look at the keys again
; D 4162 B0 00 99       GAL KEYS
; MOVE:
; D 4165 8C 03          TESTXZ R3              Which way?
; D 4167 A0 01 97       IFTRUEI LEFT
; D 416A 50 12 01       ADDXYZ R1 R2 -> R1     Right: the offset grows by S
; D 416D 88 18          TESTGXY R1 R8          past 80?
; D 416F A1 01 76       IFFALSEI RWRAP
; D 4172 53 01 00 50    SUBXI R1 0050          wrap it
; RWRAP:
; D 4176 11 09 00 50    LOADXI R9 0050
; D 417A 51 91 09       SUBXYZ R9 R1 -> R9     R9 = 80 - X,
; D 417D 88 98          TESTGXY R9 R8
; D 417F A1 01 86       IFFALSEI RCOL
; D 4182 53 09 00 50    SUBXI R9 0050          mod 80: the picture column now at screen column 1
; RCOL:
; D 4186 10 00 40       LOADAI 0040            The line control: ESC [ S @ - insert S blanks
; D 4189 2F 00 0D 85    WRITEIDX R0 0D85
; D 418D 10 00 00       LOADAI 0000            and it ends there - the cells go in at column 1
; D 4190 2F 00 0D 86    WRITEIDX R0 0D86
; D 4194 B0 01 CE       GAL SHIFT
; LEFT:
; D 4197 89 12          TESTLXY R1 R2          Left: would the offset go below 0?
; D 4199 A1 01 A0       IFFALSEI LWRAP
; D 419C 52 01 00 50    ADDXI R1 0050          then wrap it first
; LWRAP:
; D 41A0 51 12 01       SUBXYZ R1 R2 -> R1     the offset shrinks by S
; D 41A3 11 09 00 A0    LOADXI R9 00A0
; D 41A7 51 92 09       SUBXYZ R9 R2 -> R9
; D 41AA 51 91 09       SUBXYZ R9 R1 -> R9     R9 = 160 - S - X,
; D 41AD 88 98          TESTGXY R9 R8
; D 41AF A1 01 B6       IFFALSEI LCOL
; D 41B2 53 09 00 50    SUBXI R9 0050          mod 80: the picture column now at screen column 81-S
; LCOL:
; D 41B6 10 00 50       LOADAI 0050            The line control: ESC [ S P - delete S cells,
; D 41B9 2F 00 0D 85    WRITEIDX R0 0D85
; D 41BD 10 00 1B       LOADAI 001B            then ESC [ 7 u C - forward 80-S, to column 81-S
; D 41C0 2F 00 0D 86    WRITEIDX R0 0D86
; D 41C4 10 00 3A       LOADAI 003A            u = '0' + 10 - S
; D 41C7 47 02          SUBAX R2
; D 41C9 25             COPYMAA
; D 41CA 2F 00 0D 89    WRITEIDX R0 0D89
; SHIFT:
; D 41CE 22 02          COPYXA 02              S as its digit, into the line control
; D 41D0 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 41D3 2F 00 0D 84    WRITEIDX R0 0D84
; D 41D7 11 0D 00 01    LOADXI R13 0001        Cursor to the line ABOVE the picture: every line
; D 41DB 11 0E 00 01    LOADXI R14 0001        control starts with CR LF, which steps down one
; D 41DF BD 02 69       CALL POSXY
; D 41E2 11 04 00 15    LOADXI R4 0015         Picture lines to shift
; D 41E6 11 05 00 59    LOADXI R5 0059         Grid row of the first one
; LINE:
; D 41EA 11 0B 0D 80    LOADXI R11 0D80
; D 41EE C1 0B          PRINTSTR R11           CR LF, then the line moves in the terminal
; D 41F0 50 59 0A       ADDXYZ R5 R9 -> R10    Grid index of the first wrapped cell
; D 41F3 23 00 27       COPYXY R2 -> R7        S cells to paint
; CELL:
; D 41F6 2E 0A 03 00    READIDX R10 0300       The grid holds the low byte of the cell's string
; D 41FA 4E 0D 00       ADDAI 0D00             in page $0D
; D 41FD 21 0B          COPYAX 0B
; D 41FF C1 0B          PRINTSTR R11           blank, lit, or a caption letter
; D 4201 42 0A          INCX R10               Next cell - never past the row's copied tail
; D 4203 43 07          DECX R7
; D 4205 8C 07          TESTXZ R7
; D 4207 A1 01 F6       IFFALSEI CELL
; D 420A 52 05 00 59    ADDXI R5 0059          Next line: the grid row moves on 89
; D 420E 43 04          DECX R4
; D 4210 8C 04          TESTXZ R4
; D 4212 A1 01 EA       IFFALSEI LINE
; D 4215 B0 00 99       GAL KEYS               Frame done - look at the keys
; QUIT:
; D 4218 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B             Back to normal video
; D 421A CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B
; D 421C CA 30          SEROUTI 30
; D 421E CA 6D          SEROUTI 6D
; D 4220 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B             Show the cursor again
; D 4222 CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B
; D 4224 CA 3F          SEROUTI 3F
; D 4226 CA 32          SEROUTI 32
; D 4228 CA 35          SEROUTI 35
; D 422A CA 68          SEROUTI 68
; D 422C CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B             Clear the screen
; D 422E CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B
; D 4230 CA 32          SEROUTI 32
; D 4232 CA 4A          SEROUTI 4A
; D 4234 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B             Cursor home
; D 4236 CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B
; D 4238 CA 48          SEROUTI 48
; D 423A F0 00 00       BREAK                  End of program
; SPEED:
; D 423D 11 0D 00 01    LOADXI R13 0001
; D 4241 11 0E 00 01    LOADXI R14 0001
; D 4245 BD 02 69       CALL POSXY
; D 4248 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B             Clear the old marks
; D 424A CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B
; D 424C CA 4B          SEROUTI 4B
; D 424E 23 00 27       COPYXY R2 -> R7
; SPD:
; D 4251 8C 07          TESTXZ R7
; D 4253 A0 02 67       IFTRUEI SRET
; D 4256 10 00 3C       LOADAI 003C            '<'
; D 4259 8C 03          TESTXZ R3
; D 425B A0 02 61       IFTRUEI SOUT
; D 425E 10 00 3E       LOADAI 003E            '>'
; SOUT:
; D 4261 C9             SEROUT
; D 4262 43 07          DECX R7
; D 4264 B0 02 51       GAL SPD
; SRET:
; D 4267 BE 00          RETURN
; POSXY:
; D 4269 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B             ESC
; D 426B CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B             [
; D 426D 4D DF          DIVXY R13 R15
; D 426F 25             COPYMAA
; D 4270 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 4273 C9             SEROUT                 Tens
; D 4274 27             COPYREMA
; D 4275 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 4278 C9             SEROUT                 Units
; D 4279 CA 3B          SEROUTI 3B             ;
; D 427B 4D EF          DIVXY R14 R15
; D 427D 25             COPYMAA
; D 427E 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 4281 C9             SEROUT                 Tens
; D 4282 27             COPYREMA
; D 4283 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 4286 C9             SEROUT                 Units
; D 4287 CA 48          SEROUTI 48             H
; D 4289 BE 00          RETURN

